<p>In the latest escalation, the United States struck the B1 bridge between Tehran and Karaj on Thursday, and President Trump said more attacks on Iranian infrastructure could follow unless Tehran agrees to US terms. Iranian officials said the strike killed eight people and wounded 95, though some outlets noted those figures could not be independently verified because reporting restrictions inside Iran limit outside access. Iran answered with fresh missile attacks on Israel and threats of further retaliation against US and allied targets across the region. The bridge strike signaled a new focus on infrastructure after nearly five weeks of war that has spread across the Middle East, disrupting energy flows and rattling global markets. At the same time, Washington said President Trump remains open to diplomacy, even as strain on energy shipping and financial markets keeps other governments focused on containing the conflict&#x27;s broader economic fallout.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/9CbaGpF_7Kl24JSn5A55n4awPWk33A81nPc6I1TfLp03iEkFzg_sZNXQK7BvW06TdBByKySO6cXNlNhF2g8CgenQcUsSgHFxUZK1nwcPGYHizZ5lc6Tw7-wg4ndMdUvAWfQ1-kKVEcoEs4L1dymMLX4pn7ZjQSYQoYmewjaYvskZ7MYJvDUaCSK9BWaPNdIO5X2E-O0H-AKcbk-ZBfnMiC38fv0T9TZx_SSbLMcWvOW9NPSjpfgj7GqKaghwOgy777oZ-WmWRsk9C4pcBg' alt='Smoke rises following a strike in Tehran amid the U.S.-Israeli war with Iran, April 1, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Holiday timing: Euronews reported that families had gathered near the bridge for Nature Day celebrations when the strike hit, adding to the civilian toll reported by Iranian authorities.</li><li>Not operating: The New York Times said a local Iranian official described the mountain bridge as not yet in operation, with casualties among people nearby rather than on an active traffic route.</li><li>War law: Legal experts cited by Al-Monitor and the South China Morning Post said President Trump&#x27;s public threats to destroy bridges and power plants raised alarms about possible violations of the laws of war, especially if civilian infrastructure is deliberately targeted.</li><li>Market pressure: Semafor reported that oil prices rose after President Trump said US forces would hit Iran &quot;extremely hard,&quot; while financial markets remained uneasy despite the tougher rhetoric.</li></ul><blockquote>The biggest bridge in Iran comes tumbling down, never to be used again - Much more to follow! It is time for Iran to make a deal before it is too late, and there is nothing left of what still could become a great country! - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US State Department: The department accused Iran of attacking civilian sites and used that claim to justify keeping pressure on Tehran, while still saying diplomacy remains available if Iran changes course. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/2/as-war-drags-on-us-reiterates-trump-open-to-diplomacy-with-iran'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Mohammad Javad Zarif: Iran&#x27;s former foreign minister said Tehran should &quot;declare victory&quot; and make a deal, a notable public argument from within Iran&#x27;s political establishment for using the current moment to negotiate. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2026/4/3/iran-war-live-trump-warns-assault-on-infrastructure-hasnt-even-started'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Iranian officials: Officials said they would rebuild the bridge and argued the strike damaged America&#x27;s standing rather than Iran&#x27;s resolve, framing the attack as a reason for public defiance rather than concession. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/3/iran-vows-retaliation-after-deadly-us-strike-on-bridge-in-karaj'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>UK and France: Semafor said Trump&#x27;s rhetoric did little to calm markets and effectively left the work of restoring confidence in Hormuz transit to allies, with London and Paris taking the diplomatic lead. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/02/2026/us-destroys-key-iran-bridge-as-trump-threats-fail-to-calm-markets'>Semafor</a>)</li><li>Regional analysts: Experts interviewed by PBS said Gulf states and European allies are trying to avoid being pulled deeper into the conflict because they fear a wider regional war and longer disruption to energy and shipping routes. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/how-gulf-nations-and-european-allies-are-responding-to-trumps-iran-address'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/02/2026/us-destroys-key-iran-bridge-as-trump-threats-fail-to-calm-markets'>US destroys key Iran bridge as Trump threats fail to calm markets</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2026/4/3/iran-war-live-trump-warns-assault-on-infrastructure-hasnt-even-started'>Iran war live: Ex-FM Zarif says Tehran should ‘declare victory, make deal’</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/israel-under-fire-iran-missiles-trump-issues-new-warning'>Israel under fire from Iran missiles as Trump issues new warning</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3348912/trumps-stone-age-threats-against-iran-spark-war-crimes-alarm'>Trump’s ‘Stone Age’ threats against Iran spark war crimes alarm</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/02/trump-warns-tehran-more-to-follow-after-strike-destroys-irans-largest-bridge'>Trump warns Tehran ‘more to follow’ after strike destroys Iran’s largest bridge</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-04-02-0700/donald-trump-trump-makes-case-nation-taking-out-iran-investment-your-children-and-your-grandchildrens-future'>Trump makes case to nation — taking out Iran is &#x27;investment in your children and your grandchildren&#x27;s future&#x27;</a> - allsides.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-trump-threatens-more-strike